  "help": "<p><strong>What it does</strong></p>\n<p>This tool runs the <strong>cut</strong> unix command, which extract or delete columns from a file.</p>\n<hr class=\"docutils\" />\n<p>Field List Example:</p>\n<p><strong>1,3,7</strong> - Cut specific fields/characters.</p>\n<p><strong>3-</strong>    - Cut from the third field/character to the end of the line.</p>\n<p><strong>2-5</strong>   - Cut from the second to the fifth field/character.</p>\n<p><strong>-8</strong>    - Cut from the first to the eight field/characters.</p>\n<p>Input Example:</p>\n<pre class=\"literal-block\">\nfruit       color   price   weight\napple       red     1.4     0.5\norange      orange  1.5     0.3\nbanana      yellow  0.9     0.3\n</pre>\n<p>Output Example ( <strong>Keeping fields 1,3,4</strong> ):</p>\n<pre class=\"literal-block\">\nfruit       price   weight\napple       1.4     0.5\norange      1.5     0.3\nbanana      0.9     0.3\n</pre>\n<p>Output Example ( <strong>Discarding field 2</strong> ):</p>\n<pre class=\"literal-block\">\nfruit       price   weight\napple       1.4     0.5\norange      1.5     0.3\nbanana      0.9     0.3\n</pre>\n<p>Output Example ( <strong>Keeping 3 characters</strong> ):</p>\n<pre class=\"literal-block\">\nfru\napp\nora\nban\n</pre>\n<p>&#64;REFERENCES&#64;</p>\n",
  "help_format": "restructuredtext",
